{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SsgGaB5saDAevpXAGMrPA3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Reframe为''Structured pruning breaks RLVR alignment — a systematic\n2\t  empirical study''。放弃mechanism-level claim。核心贡献缩减为: (1) 首次documenting GRPO reward-accuracy\n3\t  decoupling; (2) 首次documenting GRPO training collapse on structurally pruned models（即使梯度不clean）;\n4\t  (3) Empirical recommendation: SFT-only recovery。RASP降为pruning variant而非方法贡献。论文从mechanism\n5\t  paper变为empirical failure analysis + practical warning。'\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: Full GSM8K Eval Baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20\n8\t  plan_id: plan_001\n9\t  description: Full test set (N=1319) eval for all three conditions at 20% sparsity\n10\t  expected_results:\n11\t    unpruned_accuracy: 0.8127\n12\t    rasp_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.31\n13\t    standard_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.27\n14\t    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 4.0\n15\t    rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.38\n16\t    ci_width_pp: 2.5\n17\t  result_rationale: 已有N=100数据(RASP 31% vs Standard 27%)在full eval下只能微幅收敛。4pp gap在N=1319下仍不显著(p≈0.38)，因为post-prune\n18\t    accuracy本身variance大、两者都在random-ish低准确率区间。Worst档下这个gap不构成meaningful difference。\n19\t  tables:\n20\t  - name: 'Table: Post-prune accuracy (N=1319)'\n21\t    rows:\n22\t    - method: Unpruned\n23\t      accuracy: 81.27%\n24\t      stderr: ±1.07pp\n25\t    - method: RASP-20%\n26\t      accuracy: 30.5%\n27\t      stderr: ±2.54pp\n28\t    - method: Standard-20%\n29\t      accuracy: 27.1%\n30\t      stderr: ±2.45pp\n31\t  figures_description:\n32\t  - Bar chart showing post-prune accuracy. Error bars overlap heavily for RASP vs\n33\t    Standard.\n34\t  analysis: Post-prune gap不显著，不能claim RASP preserves more reasoning capacity pre-recovery。两者都严重degraded到接近random\n35\t    baseline (GSM8K ≈ 0% for truly random)。\n36\t- name: Full GSM8K Eval All Recovered Models\n37\t  plan_id: plan_004\n38\t  description: N=1319 eval for SFT-recovered and GRPO-recovered models (RASP_20, Standard_20,\n39\t    unpruned)\n40\t  expected_results:\n41\t    sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n42\t    sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n43\t    sft_gap_20_pp: 2.2\n44\t    sft_gap_20_p_value: 0.25\n45\t    grpo_rasp_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n46\t    grpo_standard_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n47\t    grpo_unpruned_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n48\t    grpo_unpruned_delta_vs_sft: 0.0\n49\t  result_rationale: '这些数据已实际收集完毕。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)在worst档下被视为不显著。GRPO对所有模型都不提升accuracy（unpruned:\n50\t    0.00pp, Standard: -0.38pp, RASP: -0.84pp），这是strong negative result但不需要RASP-specific解释。Collapse\n51\t    dynamics差异（RASP step10 vs Standard step60）在20%下存在，但worst档的核心问题是这个gradient在25%下消失。'\n52\t  tables:\n53\t  - name: 'Table 1: Recovery accuracy comparison (N=1319)'\n54\t    rows:\n55\t    - condition: Unpruned SFT\n56\t      accuracy: 81.27%\n57\t      grpo_accuracy: 81.27%\n58\t      delta: 0.00pp\n59\t    - condition: RASP-20% SFT\n60\t      accuracy: 61.49%\n61\t      grpo_accuracy: 60.65%\n62\t      delta: -0.84pp\n63\t    - condition: Standard-20% SFT\n64\t      accuracy: 59.29%\n65\t      grpo_accuracy: 58.91%\n66\t      delta: -0.38pp\n67\t  figures_description:\n68\t  - 'Paired bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for each condition. GRPO never exceeds\n69\t    SFT for any condition.'\n70\t  analysis: Universal reward-accuracy decoupling confirmed。但SFT gap (RASP vs Standard)\n71\t    在p=0.25下insufficient to support Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff claim。论文只能claim\n72\t    GRPO failure是universal，而非pruning-method-specific。\n73\t- name: GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\n74\t  plan_id: plan_005\n75\t  description: 'GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO\n76\t    full pipeline'\n77\t  expected_results:\n78\t    grasp_post_prune_accuracy: 0.07\n79\t    grasp_post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n80\t    grasp_post_grpo_step30_accuracy: 0.39\n81\t    grasp_grpo_collapse_step: 5\n82\t    grasp_grpo_final_reward: 0.012\n83\t    grasp_grpo_frac_zero_std_final: 0.97\n84\t  result_rationale: GRASPrune在post-prune (7%)和post-SFT (41%)都远低于RASP(31%→61%)和Standard(27%→59%)。这是因为GRASPrune的gate-based\n85\t    selection在reasoning model上suboptimal——它优化一般loss而非reasoning trace。在worst档下，GRASPrune\n86\t    GRPO会比RASP更快collapse(step 5)，但这不提供diagnostic value因为GRASPrune本身就是inferior pruning，collapse快是trivial结论。这个baseline反而削弱了RASP的novelty——如果所有结构化剪枝方法的GRPO都collapse，那collapse不是RASP-specific\n87\t    insight。\n88\t  tables:\n89\t  - name: 'Table: GRASPrune pipeline comparison'\n90\t    rows:\n91\t    - stage: Post-prune\n92\t      grasp: 7%\n93\t      rasp: 31%\n94\t      standard: 27%\n95\t    - stage: Post-SFT\n96\t      grasp: 41%\n97\t      rasp: 61.5%\n98\t      standard: 59.3%\n99\t    - stage: Post-GRPO\n100\t      grasp: 39%\n101\t      rasp: 60.7%\n102\t      standard: 58.9%\n103\t    - stage: GRPO collapse step\n104\t      grasp: ~5\n105\t      rasp: ~10\n106\t      standard: ~60\n107\t  figures_description:\n108\t  - 'Training dynamics plot: GRASPrune collapses immediately (step 5), joining RASP\n109\t    and Standard in universal GRPO failure pattern.'\n110\t  analysis: 'GRASPrune数据confirms所有structured pruning methods的GRPO都fail，但severity ordering\n111\t    (GRASPrune < RASP < Standard)在worst档下被解释为trivially correlated with post-SFT quality而非redundancy-specific\n112\t    mechanism。Reviewer会argue: ''collapse speed simply tracks model quality, not structural\n113\t    damage type''。'\n114\t- name: Multi-seed Post-prune Eval\n115\t  plan_id: plan_006\n116\t  description: 5 seeds (incl. seed 42) for RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune eval,\n117\t    variance estimation\n118\t  expected_results:\n119\t    rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.305\n120\t    rasp_20_std: 0.018\n121\t    standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.278\n122\t    standard_20_std: 0.022\n123\t    mean_gap_pp: 2.7\n124\t    paired_t_p_value: 0.15\n125\t    cohens_d: 0.42\n126\t  result_rationale: Post-prune accuracy受calibration sample variance影响。5 seeds下RASP\n127\t    mean ≈ 30.5%, Standard mean ≈ 27.8%, gap ~2.7pp。但std较大(1.8-2.2pp)导致paired-t test\n128\t    p≈0.15。Worst档下reviewers会argue这个gap不足以支持CKA-aware scoring的优越性。Cohen's d=0.42 (medium\n129\t    effect)不够convincing for a core method claim。\n130\t  tables:\n131\t  - name: 'Table: Multi-seed post-prune accuracy'\n132\t    rows:\n133\t    - seed: 42\n134\t      rasp: 31%\n135\t      standard: 27%\n136\t    - seed: 123\n137\t      rasp: 29%\n138\t      standard: 28%\n139\t    - seed: 456\n140\t      rasp: 32%\n141\t      standard: 30%\n142\t    - seed: 789\n143\t      rasp: 28%\n144\t      standard: 26%\n145\t    - seed: 1024\n146\t      rasp: 32.5%\n147\t      standard: 28%\n148\t  figures_description:\n149\t  - Box plot showing overlapping distributions of RASP vs Standard across 5 seeds.\n150\t    Medians differ by ~3pp but IQRs overlap.\n151\t  analysis: Multi-seed证据weak。Gap存在但不robust (p=0.15)。在worst档下这strengthens the narrative\n152\t    that CKA-aware scoring的marginal benefit不justify方法复杂度。\n153\t- name: Scoring Ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\n154\t  plan_id: plan_007\n155\t  description: 'Ablation: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning at 20% sparsity'\n156\t  expected_results:\n157\t    magnitude_only_accuracy: 0.26\n158\t    gradient_only_accuracy: 0.29\n159\t    random_pruning_accuracy: 0.18\n160\t    rasp_accuracy_ref: 0.31\n161\t    standard_accuracy_ref: 0.27\n162\t    gradient_vs_rasp_gap: 2.0\n163\t    gradient_vs_rasp_p_value: 0.41\n164\t  result_rationale: Worst档下，gradient-only(即Standard的核心——importance scoring)已达到29%，接近RASP的31%。CKA\n165\t    modulation仅额外贡献~2pp，这在N=100下完全不显著(p=0.41)。Magnitude-only(26%)和Standard(27%)几乎相同，说明importance\n166\t    metric差异在post-prune这个极低accuracy regime下noise-dominated。Random(18%)是唯一clearly worse的，但这是trivial——任何informed\n167\t    method都应该beat random。Ablation结果undermine CKA的独立贡献。\n168\t  tables:\n169\t  - name: 'Table: Scoring method ablation (20% sparsity, N=100)'\n170\t    rows:\n171\t    - method: RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\n172\t      accuracy: 31%\n173\t      stderr: ±4.6%\n174\t    - method: Gradient-only (I)\n175\t      accuracy: 29%\n176\t      stderr: ±4.5%\n177\t    - method: Standard (importance)\n178\t      accuracy: 27%\n179\t      stderr: ±4.4%\n180\t    - method: Magnitude-only\n181\t      accuracy: 26%\n182\t      stderr: ±4.4%\n183\t    - method: Random\n184\t      accuracy: 18%\n185\t      stderr: ±3.8%\n186\t  figures_description:\n187\t  - Horizontal bar chart with error bars. All informed methods cluster around 26-31%,\n188\t    random at 18%. Error bars heavily overlap for all non-random methods.\n189\t  analysis: CKA modulation的贡献被noise淹没。Worst档叙事：RASP's CKA component is at best marginal\n190\t    (2pp over gradient-only, p=0.41)。不足以支持CKA作为method contribution。\n191\t- name: Per-structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\n192\t  plan_id: plan_008\n193\t  description: Per-head F(h) vs activation change after recovery, mixed-effects regression\n194\t  expected_results:\n195\t    pearson_r_fh_vs_activation_change: 0.12\n196\t    spearman_rho: 0.09\n197\t    mixed_effects_p_value_fh: 0.31\n198\t    variance_explained_by_fh: 0.014\n199\t    weight_norm_variance_explained: 0.08\n200\t    gradient_importance_variance_explained: 0.11\n201\t  result_rationale: Worst档下，F(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy）与recovery后的activation\n202\t    change几乎无correlation (r=0.12)。Mixed-effects model中F(h)不显著(p=0.31)，且解释方差仅1.4%——远低于简单的weight\n203\t    norm (8%)或gradient importance (11%)。这demolishes CKA作为'predicting recoverability'的诊断工具的claim。如果functional\n204\t    redundancy不predict recoverability，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的机制基础就不存在。\n205\t  tables:\n206\t  - name: 'Table: Mixed-effects regression coefficients'\n207\t    rows:\n208\t    - predictor: F(h) (CKA redundancy)\n209\t      beta: '0.034'\n210\t      p_value: '0.31'\n211\t      R²_partial: '0.014'\n212\t    - predictor: Weight norm\n213\t      beta: '0.089'\n214\t      p_value: '0.02'\n215\t      R²_partial: '0.08'\n216\t    - predictor: Gradient importance\n217\t      beta: '0.102'\n218\t      p_value: '0.008'\n219\t      R²_partial: '0.11'\n220\t    - predictor: Activation magnitude\n221\t      beta: '0.076'\n222\t      p_value: '0.04'\n223\t      R²_partial: '0.06'\n224\t  figures_description:\n225\t  - 'Scatter plot: F(h) vs activation change, color-coded by layer. No visible trend,\n226\t    points scattered. R²=0.014 annotated.'\n227\t  analysis: CKA-based redundancy metric不predict recovery behavior。在worst档下这是致命的——RASP的理论基础(redundant\n228\t    structures are safely removable for SFT)没有per-structure evidence支撑。\n229\t- name: SFT-only Recovery Comparison\n230\t  plan_id: plan_009\n231\t  description: Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20), SFT only, same data budget.\n232\t    Tests recovery paradigm interaction.\n233\t  expected_results:\n234\t    sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n235\t    sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n236\t    sft_gap_pp: 2.2\n237\t    sft_gap_p_value: 0.25\n238\t    sft_rasp_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n239\t    sft_standard_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n240\t  result_rationale: 这个实验实际上已经完成（plan_002的SFT就是SFT-only recovery）。Worst档下结果不变：RASP\n241\t    61.49% vs Standard 59.29%，gap 2.2pp, p=0.25。Loss curves几乎identical（都converge到0.64）。不显著的SFT\n242\t    gap意味着'CKA-aware pruning benefits SFT recovery'这个claim不成立。如果SFT gap都不存在，Redundancy-Stability\n243\t    Tradeoff（SFT favors removing redundancy, RLVR needs it）的SFT侧就是null。\n244\t  tables:\n245\t  - name: 'Table: SFT-only recovery (N=1319)'\n246\t    rows:\n247\t    - method: RASP-20%\n248\t      sft_accuracy: 61.49%\n249\t      sft_loss: '0.64'\n250\t    - method: Standard-20%\n251\t      sft_accuracy: 59.29%\n252\t      sft_loss: '0.64'\n253\t    - method: Gap\n254\t      delta: +2.20pp\n255\t      p_value: '0.25'\n256\t  figures_description:\n257\t  - Loss curves for RASP vs Standard SFT recovery — virtually identical trajectories,\n258\t    both converging to 0.64.\n259\t  analysis: SFT gap不显著。Worst档叙事：无法claim RASP对SFT recovery有advantage，因此Redundancy-Stability\n260\t    Tradeoff的一侧(SFT favors RASP)不成立。\n261\t- name: 25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Full Pipeline\n262\t  plan_id: plan_010\n263\t  description: '25% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both RASP and Standard'\n264\t  expected_results:\n265\t    rasp_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.21\n266\t    standard_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.16\n267\t    rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.52\n268\t    standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n269\t    sft_gap_25_pp: 0.75\n270\t    sft_gap_25_p_value: 0.35\n271\t    grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n272\t    grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 6\n273\t    grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.011\n274\t    grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.015\n275\t    grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n276\t    grpo_standard_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.96\n277\t    collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: 0.67\n278\t  result_rationale: '25%是worst档的critical sparsity。Post-prune: RASP 21% vs Standard\n279\t    16%（已confirmed）。Post-SFT: RASP ~52% vs Standard ~51.25%（已有Standard数据），gap缩小到<1pp\n280\t    (p=0.35)——因为higher sparsity下SFT recovery能力更受限于absolute damage而非which structures\n281\t    were removed。GRPO: 关键——两者都在≤10步内collapse。RASP step 4, Standard step 6，ratio仅0.67（不是20%下的6x差距）。这是因为25%\n282\t    sparsity下两个模型的exploration capacity都已被破坏到临界值以下，collapse变成near-deterministic而非structure-dependent。Severity\n283\t    gradient消失——无法区分''redundancy removal causing fast collapse'' vs ''general over-pruning\n284\t    causing universal collapse''。'\n285\t  tables:\n286\t  - name: 'Table: 25% sparsity pipeline comparison'\n287\t    rows:\n288\t    - stage: Post-prune\n289\t      rasp_25: 21%\n290\t      standard_25: 16%\n291\t    - stage: Post-SFT\n292\t      rasp_25: 52%\n293\t      standard_25: 51.25%\n294\t    - stage: Post-SFT gap\n295\t      delta: +0.75pp\n296\t      p_value: '0.35'\n297\t    - stage: GRPO collapse step\n298\t      rasp_25: ~4\n299\t      standard_25: ~6\n300\t    - stage: GRPO final frac_zero_std\n301\t      rasp_25: '0.98'\n302\t      standard_25: '0.96'\n303\t  - name: 'Table: Collapse gradient comparison across sparsity'\n304\t    rows:\n305\t    - sparsity: 20%\n306\t      rasp_collapse: step 10\n307\t      standard_collapse: step 60\n308\t      ratio: 6.0x\n309\t    - sparsity: 25%\n310\t      rasp_collapse: step 4\n311\t      standard_collapse: step 6\n312\t      ratio: 1.5x\n313\t  figures_description:\n314\t  - 'Training dynamics overlay: RASP-25% and Standard-25% frac_zero_std curves nearly\n315\t    overlapping, both reaching 0.95+ by step 8. Contrast with 20% where curves diverge\n316\t    dramatically.'\n317\t  - 'Collapse ratio vs sparsity plot: ratio drops from 6x at 20% to 1.5x at 25%, suggesting\n318\t    the diagnostic value disappears at higher sparsity.'\n319\t  analysis: '25% sparsity完全消解了collapse severity gradient。两者都太脆弱无法sustain GRPO training。Reviewer会argue:\n320\t    ''你的diagnostic只在一个sparsity点work(20%)，换个sparsity就break——这不是robust mechanism而是coincidence。''\n321\t    SFT gap也shrink到不显著(0.75pp, p=0.35)。Worst档核心结论：Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在25%下不可观测。'\n322\t- name: 30% Sparsity Probe\n323\t  plan_id: plan_011\n324\t  description: 30% sparsity prune + eval only (no recovery) for RASP and Standard\n325\t  expected_results:\n326\t    rasp_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.08\n327\t    standard_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.06\n328\t    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.25\n329\t    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.18\n330\t    gap_pp: 2.0\n331\t    p_value: 0.55\n332\t  result_rationale: 30% sparsity下两者都接近complete collapse (8% vs 6%)。Model基本无法生成coherent\n333\t    reasoning。Gap 2pp在这个regime下meaningless——两者都是catastrophically damaged。这confirms\n334\t    25-30%是DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B structured pruning的hard ceiling，但不提供任何method-differentiating\n335\t    evidence。\n336\t  tables:\n337\t  - name: 'Table: 30% sparsity post-prune'\n338\t    rows:\n339\t    - method: RASP-30%\n340\t      accuracy: 8%\n341\t      eos_rate: 25%\n342\t      avg_len: '3200'\n343\t    - method: Standard-30%\n344\t      accuracy: 6%\n345\t      eos_rate: 18%\n346\t      avg_len: '3500'\n347\t  figures_description:\n348\t  - 'Sparsity vs post-prune accuracy curve: steep decline from 20% to 30%, both methods\n349\t    converging to near-zero.'\n350\t  analysis: Confirms sparsity ceiling但对method comparison无价值。在worst档下用作evidence that\n351\t    structured pruning has narrow useful range (practical limitation)。\n352\t- name: Extended Evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\n353\t  plan_id: plan_012\n354\t  description: Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks\n355\t  expected_results:\n356\t    rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.48\n357\t    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n358\t    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n359\t    standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.47\n360\t    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n361\t    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n362\t    unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.62\n363\t    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n364\t    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n365\t    rasp_vs_standard_mmlu_p: 0.62\n366\t    rasp_vs_standard_humaneval_p: 0.45\n367\t    rasp_vs_standard_math500_p: 0.38\n368\t  result_rationale: 'OOD benchmarks下RASP vs Standard gap同样不显著。MMLU差1pp, HumanEval差2pp,\n369\t    MATH差2pp——都在noise range内。这是因为SFT recovery是domain-agnostic的(teacher-forcing on\n370\t    GSM8K)，CKA-aware pruning的marginal structural advantage不transfer到其他tasks。Worst档下这进一步confirms\n371\t    RASP无meaningful advantage。同时，pruned vs unpruned的大幅drop (MATH: 52%→27%)表明structured\n372\t    pruning造成的reasoning能力损失是across-domain的。'\n373\t  tables:\n374\t  - name: 'Table: Extended evaluation'\n375\t    rows:\n376\t    - benchmark: MMLU\n377\t      unpruned: 62%\n378\t      rasp_20: 48%\n379\t      standard_20: 47%\n380\t      gap_pp: +1pp\n381\t      p: '0.62'\n382\t    - benchmark: HumanEval\n383\t      unpruned: 55%\n384\t      rasp_20: 35%\n385\t      standard_20: 33%\n386\t      gap_pp: +2pp\n387\t      p: '0.45'\n388\t    - benchmark: MATH-500\n389\t      unpruned: 52%\n390\t      rasp_20: 28%\n391\t      standard_20: 26%\n392\t      gap_pp: +2pp\n393\t      p: '0.38'\n394\t  figures_description:\n395\t  - 'Radar chart showing capability profile: unpruned vs RASP-20% vs Standard-20%\n396\t    across 4 benchmarks. Pruned models uniformly degraded, RASP and Standard nearly\n397\t    identical.'\n398\t  analysis: RASP advantage不generalize beyond GSM8K。在worst档下这是expected——如果GSM8K上gap都不显著，OOD上更不可能significant。但pruned\n399\t    models的uniform degradation strengthens 'structured pruning is destructive' narrative。\n400\t- name: Bonsai Baseline 20%\n401\t  plan_id: plan_013\n402\t  description: Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning at 20% sparsity\n403\t  expected_results:\n404\t    bonsai_post_prune_accuracy: 0.24\n405\t    bonsai_post_sft_accuracy: 0.56\n406\t    bonsai_post_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n407\t    bonsai_grpo_peak_reward: 0.019\n408\t    bonsai_grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.93\n409\t  result_rationale: 'Bonsai是gradient-free方法，通常在structured pruning中accuracy略低于gradient-based方法。Post-prune\n410\t    24% (between random 18% and Standard 27%)。Post-SFT recovery到56%——低于RASP(61.5%)和Standard(59.3%)但仍reasonable。GRPO\n411\t    collapse at step 8——和RASP(step 10)同量级。在worst档下，Bonsai的加入进一步demonstrates所有structured\n412\t    pruning的GRPO都collapse，且collapse speed和post-SFT quality正相关（trivialy: worse model\n413\t    = faster collapse）。不提供redundancy-specific insight。'\n414\t  tables:\n415\t  - name: 'Table: Method comparison including Bonsai'\n416\t    rows:\n417\t    - method: RASP\n418\t      post_prune: 31%\n419\t      post_sft: 61.5%\n420\t      grpo_collapse: step 10\n421\t    - method: Standard\n422\t      post_prune: 27%\n423\t      post_sft: 59.3%\n424\t      grpo_collapse: step 60\n425\t    - method: Bonsai\n426\t      post_prune: 24%\n427\t      post_sft: 56%\n428\t      grpo_collapse: step 8\n429\t    - method: GRASPrune\n430\t      post_prune: 7%\n431\t      post_sft: 41%\n432\t      grpo_collapse: step 5\n433\t  figures_description:\n434\t  - 'Scatter plot: post-SFT accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all 4 methods. Clear\n435\t    positive correlation (r=0.95) suggesting collapse speed is simply a function of\n436\t    model quality, not pruning mechanism.'\n437\t  analysis: 'Bonsai数据reveals collapse speed几乎perfectly correlates with post-SFT accuracy\n438\t    (r≈0.95)。Worst档下reviewer会argue: ''RASP collapses fast不是因为它removed redundancy,\n439\t    而是因为它happens to produce slightly lower SFT quality than Standard (61.5 vs 59.3,\n440\t    but at 25% the gap disappears and so does the collapse difference)。Collapse is\n441\t    trivially predicted by model quality, not by structural damage type。'''\n442\t- name: CKA Reliability Analysis\n443\t  plan_id: plan_014\n444\t  description: Split-half consistency + calibration size sensitivity\n445\t  expected_results:\n446\t    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.72\n447\t    cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.78\n448\t    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.85\n449\t    score_variance_across_splits: 0.15\n450\t    top_20pct_overlap_across_splits: 0.68\n451\t  result_rationale: CKA scores本身有moderate reliability (ρ=0.72 split-half)，不算terrible但也不够high\n452\t    for confident structure selection。Top-20% pruned structures只有68% overlap across\n453\t    splits——意味着32%的pruning decisions是unstable的。Calibration size从256→512→1024确实improves\n454\t    (0.78→0.85)，但512 (我们用的) 仍有notable instability。Worst档下这undermines RASP scoring的reliability——如果CKA\n455\t    scores themselves are noisy，基于它们的pruning decision也是noisy的。\n456\t  tables:\n457\t  - name: 'Table: CKA reliability metrics'\n458\t    rows:\n459\t    - metric: Split-half Spearman ρ\n460\t      value: '0.72'\n461\t    - metric: Cal-256 vs Cal-512 rank corr\n462\t      value: '0.78'\n463\t    - metric: Cal-512 vs Cal-1024 rank corr\n464\t      value: '0.85'\n465\t    - metric: Top-20% set overlap (split-half)\n466\t      value: 68%\n467\t  figures_description:\n468\t  - Heatmap of structure rankings across 5 split-half replications. Visible inconsistency\n469\t    in middle-ranked structures.\n470\t  analysis: CKA reliability是acceptable but not high。32% decision instability在worst档下被interpret为：RASP的marginal\n471\t    advantage可能just是particular calibration sample的artifact而非stable structural property。\n472\t- name: Alpha Sensitivity Ablation\n473\t  plan_id: plan_015\n474\t  description: α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} sweep in RASP scoring at 20% sparsity, post-prune\n475\t    + post-SFT eval\n476\t  expected_results:\n477\t    alpha_0_post_prune: 0.27\n478\t    alpha_0_post_sft: 0.64\n479\t    alpha_0p25_post_prune: 0.23\n480\t    alpha_0p25_post_sft: 0.58\n481\t    alpha_0p5_post_prune: 0.22\n482\t    alpha_0p5_post_sft: 0.55\n483\t    alpha_1p0_post_prune: 0.31\n484\t    alpha_1p0_post_sft: 0.57\n485\t    alpha_2p0_post_prune: 0.36\n486\t    alpha_2p0_post_sft: 0.62\n487\t    optimal_alpha_post_prune: 2.0\n488\t    optimal_alpha_post_sft: 0.0\n489\t    correlation_postprune_vs_postsft: -0.45\n490\t  result_rationale: '已有post-prune数据(α=0:27%, α=0.25:23%, α=0.5:22%, α=1:31%, α=2:36%)。Post-SFT数据在worst档下shows反转：α=0(即Standard，无CKA)给出最高post-SFT(64%)，而α=2(强CKA\n491\t    weighting, 最高post-prune)给出62%。α和post-SFT accuracy无单调关系，且post-prune和post-SFT accuracy\n492\t    negatively correlated (r=-0.45)——高post-prune不predict高post-SFT。这is devastating:\n493\t    RASP的CKA modulation optimizes wrong proxy。保留high-CKA structures helps immediate\n494\t    post-prune accuracy但doesn''t help (甚至slightly hurts) SFT recovery。'\n495\t  tables:\n496\t  - name: 'Table: Alpha ablation full pipeline'\n497\t    rows:\n498\t    - alpha: 0.0 (=Standard)\n499\t      post_prune: 27%\n500\t      post_sft: 64%\n501\t      post_sft_ci: ±4.7%\n502\t    - alpha: '0.25'\n503\t      post_prune: 23%\n504\t      post_sft: 58%\n505\t      post_sft_ci: ±4.9%\n506\t    - alpha: '0.5'\n507\t      post_prune: 22%\n508\t      post_sft: 55%\n509\t      post_sft_ci: ±5.0%\n510\t    - alpha: 1.0 (=RASP)\n511\t      post_prune: 31%\n512\t      post_sft: 57%\n513\t      post_sft_ci: ±5.0%\n514\t    - alpha: '2.0'\n515\t      post_prune: 36%\n516\t      post_sft: 62%\n517\t      post_sft_ci: ±4.9%\n518\t  figures_description:\n519\t  - 'Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) and α vs post-SFT accuracy\n520\t    (non-monotonic/U-shape). Shows CKA helps post-prune but not post-SFT.'\n521\t  - 'Scatter: post-prune accuracy vs post-SFT accuracy across α values. Negative or\n522\t    null correlation.'\n523\t  analysis: 'α ablation是worst档最damaging的实验。Post-prune accuracy和post-SFT accuracy decouple——CKA\n524\t    optimization of post-prune is a wrong objective。α=0 (no CKA, Standard) achieves\n525\t    highest post-SFT despite lowest post-prune。RASP''s core insight (''remove redundant\n526\t    structures because they''re safely recoverable'') is empirically falsified: recovering\n527\t    redundant-structure-preserving models is NOT easier。'\n528\t- name: Inference Speedup Benchmark\n529\t  plan_id: plan_016\n530\t  description: Wall-clock latency + throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\n531\t  expected_results:\n532\t    dense_latency_ms_per_token: 18.5\n533\t    rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.2\n534\t    standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.0\n535\t    dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 54.1\n536\t    rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 61.7\n537\t    standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 62.5\n538\t    speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.14\n539\t    speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.16\n540\t    memory_reduction_pct: 18.5\n541\t  result_rationale: '20% structured pruning只给14-16% speedup。这是因为：(1) MLP-only pruning\n542\t    (attn groups未被pruned) 限制了speedup ceiling; (2) GPU利用率在batch_size=1时不是memory-bound;\n543\t    (3) Structured pruning的实际speedup远低于theoretical FLOP reduction (20%)因为kernel launch\n544\t    overhead和memory bandwidth不是线性关系。Worst档下1.14-1.16x speedup is disappointing——不足以justify\n545\t    20pp+ accuracy loss (81%→61%)。Reviewer: ''you lose 20pp accuracy for 14% speedup\n546\t    — no practitioner would make this trade。'''\n547\t  tables:\n548\t  - name: 'Table: Inference efficiency'\n549\t    rows:\n550\t    - model: Dense (7.6B)\n551\t      latency_ms: '18.5'\n552\t      throughput: 54.1 tok/s\n553\t      memory_gb: '15.2'\n554\t    - model: RASP-20% (6.2B)\n555\t      latency_ms: '16.2'\n556\t      throughput: 61.7 tok/s\n557\t      memory_gb: '12.4'\n558\t    - model: Standard-20% (6.2B)\n559\t      latency_ms: '16.0'\n560\t      throughput: 62.5 tok/s\n561\t      memory_gb: '12.4'\n562\t  figures_description:\n563\t  - 'Bar chart: speedup factor vs accuracy retention. 1.14x speedup at 76% accuracy\n564\t    retention — poor Pareto position.'\n565\t  analysis: Inference speedup insufficient to justify accuracy cost。Worst档下这weaken\n566\t    practical motivation：如果structured pruning只给14% speedup with 25% accuracy loss，research\n567\t    question本身的relevance被questioned。需要在paper中reframe为'studying fundamental interaction'而非'practical\n568\t    compression method'。\n569\t- name: Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\n570\t  plan_id: plan_017\n571\t  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%, eval + SFT → GRPO\n572\t  expected_results:\n573\t    unstructured_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.72\n574\t    unstructured_20_post_sft_accuracy: 0.79\n575\t    unstructured_20_grpo_accuracy: 0.79\n576\t    unstructured_20_grpo_collapse: false\n577\t    unstructured_20_grpo_steps_stable: 100\n578\t    unstructured_20_grpo_final_reward: 0.55\n579\t  result_rationale: 'Unstructured pruning at 20% preserves大部分accuracy (72% post-prune\n580\t    vs structured 27-31%)因为individual weight zeroing比removing entire structures damage\n581\t    far less。Post-SFT recovery到79%接近dense baseline (81%)。关键：GRPO在unstructured pruned\n582\t    model上NOT collapse——100 steps stable, reward reaches 0.55。这directly refutes ''pruning\n583\t    breaks RLVR''的general claim，narrowing it to''STRUCTURED pruning breaks RLVR''。In\n584\t    worst档: 这是double-edged。一方面narrows scope (only structured matters)；另一方面reviewer可能argue\n585\t    ''if unstructured doesn''t collapse, your finding is about model capacity, not\n586\t    redundancy — 20% structured removes much more effective capacity than 20% unstructured''。'\n587\t  tables:\n588\t  - name: 'Table: Structured vs Unstructured comparison'\n589\t    rows:\n590\t    - method: Dense\n591\t      post_prune: 81%\n592\t      post_sft: 81%\n593\t      grpo_collapse: 'No'\n594\t      grpo_accuracy: 81%\n595\t    - method: Unstructured-20%\n596\t      post_prune: 72%\n597\t      post_sft: 79%\n598\t      grpo_collapse: 'No'\n599\t      grpo_accuracy: 79%\n600\t    - method: RASP-Structured-20%\n601\t      post_prune: 31%\n602\t      post_sft: 61.5%\n603\t      grpo_collapse: Step 10\n604\t      grpo_accuracy: 60.7%\n605\t    - method: Standard-Structured-20%\n606\t      post_prune: 27%\n607\t      post_sft: 59.3%\n608\t      grpo_collapse: Step 60\n609\t      grpo_accuracy: 58.9%\n610\t  figures_description:\n611\t  - 'GRPO training dynamics: unstructured-20% tracks dense model (no collapse), while\n612\t    all structured methods collapse. Clear dichotomy.'\n613\t  analysis: 'Unstructured doesn''t collapse → GRPO failure是structured-pruning-specific。Worst档下reviewer会reframe为capacity\n614\t    argument: ''structured pruning removes 20% of architecture but >>20% of effective\n615\t    capacity (因为removes entire functional units)，collapse是trivially因为model太弱not因为any\n616\t    specific structural property''。这undermines Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的mechanistic\n617\t    claim进一步。'\n618\t- name: SFT OOD Eval Contingency\n619\t  plan_id: plan_018\n620\t  description: Standard SFT-recovered model (64%→59.3% GSM8K) on MATH-500 and HumanEval\n621\t  expected_results:\n622\t    standard_sft_math500: 0.22\n623\t    standard_sft_humaneval: 0.28\n624\t    rasp_sft_math500: 0.24\n625\t    rasp_sft_humaneval: 0.3\n626\t    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n627\t    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n628\t    gap_math500_pp: 2.0\n629\t    gap_humaneval_pp: 2.0\n630\t    gap_math500_p: 0.35\n631\t    gap_humaneval_p: 0.4\n632\t  result_rationale: 'OOD evaluation下RASP vs Standard gap同样tiny (2pp, p>0.35)。两个pruned\n633\t    models在harder benchmarks上都heavily degraded vs unpruned (MATH: 22-24% vs 52%, HumanEval:\n634\t    28-30% vs 55%)。这表明SFT recovery在GSM8K-domain外效果很差——recovery是domain-specific pattern\n635\t    memorization而非genuine reasoning restoration。Worst档下这进一步削弱SFT recovery作为practical\n636\t    solution的framing，但不directly影响GRPO failure narrative。'\n637\t  tables:\n638\t  - name: 'Table: OOD evaluation'\n639\t    rows:\n640\t    - benchmark: MATH-500\n641\t      unpruned: 52%\n642\t      rasp_20: 24%\n643\t      standard_20: 22%\n644\t      p_value: '0.35'\n645\t    - benchmark: HumanEval\n646\t      unpruned: 55%\n647\t      rasp_20: 30%\n648\t      standard_20: 28%\n649\t      p_value: '0.40'\n650\t    - benchmark: GSM8K\n651\t      unpruned: 81%\n652\t      rasp_20: 61.5%\n653\t      standard_20: 59.3%\n654\t      p_value: '0.25'\n655\t  figures_description:\n656\t  - 'Accuracy retention ratio (pruned/unpruned) across benchmarks. GSM8K: 75%, MATH:\n657\t    45%, HumanEval: 53%. Recovery is heavily domain-biased.'\n658\t  analysis: OOD collapse suggests SFT recovery是GSM8K-specific memorization。Worst档下这weakens\n659\t    'SFT-only recovery as practical recommendation'——如果SFT只恢复in-domain performance，recommendation的practical\n660\t    scope极其有限。\n661\t- name: Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 20% SFT Eval\n662\t  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_20\n663\t  description: Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 20% (RASP + Standard), SFT recovery, N=200\n664\t    eval\n665\t  expected_results:\n666\t    rasp_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n667\t    standard_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n668\t    gap_pp: 1.5\n669\t    gap_p_value: 0.42\n670\t  result_rationale: '已有实验数据: RASP 72.5% vs Standard 71%。Gap仅1.5pp (p=0.42)——比DeepSeek-R1上的2.2pp还小。Cross-model下CKA-aware\n671\t    pruning的advantage进一步diminish，因为Qwen-Math的architecture redundancy pattern可能不同于DeepSeek-R1-Distill。'\n672\t  tables:\n673\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-model 20% SFT'\n674\t    rows:\n675\t    - model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\n676\t      rasp: 61.5%\n677\t      standard: 59.3%\n678\t      gap: +2.2pp\n679\t    - model: Qwen2.5-Math-7B\n680\t      rasp: 72.5%\n681\t      standard: 71.0%\n682\t      gap: +1.5pp\n683\t  figures_description: []\n684\t  analysis: Cross-model SFT gap even smaller。RASP advantage不robust across models。\n685\t- name: Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 25% Full Pipeline\n686\t  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_25\n687\t  description: Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 25% (RASP + Standard), SFT + GRPO, N=200\n688\t    eval\n689\t  expected_results:\n690\t    rasp_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n691\t    standard_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n692\t    sft_gap_pp: 1.0\n693\t    sft_gap_p_value: 0.48\n694\t    grpo_rasp_25_qwen_collapse_step: 7\n695\t    grpo_standard_25_qwen_collapse_step: 8\n696\t    grpo_rasp_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.022\n697\t    grpo_standard_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.025\n698\t    collapse_ratio: 0.875\n699\t  result_rationale: 'Worst档核心: Qwen-Math上GRPO collapse差异消失。RASP step 7 vs Standard\n700\t    step 8——ratio 0.875 (within noise)。两者都rapidly collapse，无severity gradient。这directly\n701\t    falsifies ''collapse speed diagnoses structural damage type'' claim跨模型。原因：Qwen-Math的internal\n702\t    redundancy structure可能不同(more uniform, less exploitable by CKA)，或25% sparsity对Qwen-Math已经是critical\n703\t    threshold (Qwen-Math baseline更高所以25% damage也更severe in relative terms)。'\n704\t  tables:\n705\t  - name: 'Table: Qwen-Math 25% GRPO collapse comparison'\n706\t    rows:\n707\t    - model: DeepSeek-R1 25%\n708\t      rasp_collapse: step 4\n709\t      standard_collapse: step 6\n710\t      ratio: 1.5x\n711\t    - model: Qwen-Math 25%\n712\t      rasp_collapse: step 7\n713\t      standard_collapse: step 8\n714\t      ratio: 1.14x\n715\t    - model: DeepSeek-R1 20%\n716\t      rasp_collapse: step 10\n717\t      standard_collapse: step 60\n718\t      ratio: 6.0x\n719\t    - model: Qwen-Math 20%\n720\t      rasp_collapse: TBD\n721\t      standard_collapse: TBD\n722\t      ratio: TBD\n723\t  figures_description:\n724\t  - Cross-model collapse dynamics overlay. Qwen-Math RASP and Standard curves are\n725\t    indistinguishable.\n726\t  analysis: Cross-model non-reproducibility是worst档的killshot for mechanism claim。如果collapse\n727\t    gradient只在one model × one sparsity下observe，它不是generalizable mechanism而是coincidence。\n728\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87456414-598d-4dd4-8776-aaed1b39d708","uuid":"e6fe4128-1439-4c34-b08d-d2bf84865514","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:40:56.025Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Reframe为''Structured pruning breaks RLVR alignment — a systematic\n  empirical study''。放弃mechanism-level claim。核心贡献缩减为: (1) 首次documenting GRPO reward-accuracy\n  decoupling; (2) 首次documenting GRPO training collapse on structurally pruned models（即使梯度不clean）;\n  (3) Empirical recommendation: SFT-only recovery。RASP降为pruning variant而非方法贡献。论文从mechanism\n  paper变为empirical failure analysis + practical warning。'\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Full GSM8K Eval Baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: Full test set (N=1319) eval for all three conditions at 20% sparsity\n  expected_results:\n    unpruned_accuracy: 0.8127\n    rasp_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.31\n    standard_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.27\n    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 4.0\n    rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.38\n    ci_width_pp: 2.5\n  result_rationale: 已有N=100数据(RASP 31% vs Standard 27%)在full eval下只能微幅收敛。4pp gap在N=1319下仍不显著(p≈0.38)，因为post-prune\n    accuracy本身variance大、两者都在random-ish低准确率区间。Worst档下这个gap不构成meaningful difference。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Post-prune accuracy (N=1319)'\n    rows:\n    - method: Unpruned\n      accuracy: 81.27%\n      stderr: ±1.07pp\n    - method: RASP-20%\n      accuracy: 30.5%\n      stderr: ±2.54pp\n    - method: Standard-20%\n      accuracy: 27.1%\n      stderr: ±2.45pp\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart showing post-prune accuracy. Error bars overlap heavily for RASP vs\n    Standard.\n  analysis: Post-prune gap不显著，不能claim RASP preserves more reasoning capacity pre-recovery。两者都严重degraded到接近random\n    baseline (GSM8K ≈ 0% for truly random)。\n- name: Full GSM8K Eval All Recovered Models\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: N=1319 eval for SFT-recovered and GRPO-recovered models (RASP_20, Standard_20,\n    unpruned)\n  expected_results:\n    sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n    sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n    sft_gap_20_pp: 2.2\n    sft_gap_20_p_value: 0.25\n    grpo_rasp_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n    grpo_standard_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n    grpo_unpruned_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n    grpo_unpruned_delta_vs_sft: 0.0\n  result_rationale: '这些数据已实际收集完毕。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)在worst档下被视为不显著。GRPO对所有模型都不提升accuracy（unpruned:\n    0.00pp, Standard: -0.38pp, RASP: -0.84pp），这是strong negative result但不需要RASP-specific解释。Collapse\n    dynamics差异（RASP step10 vs Standard step60）在20%下存在，但worst档的核心问题是这个gradient在25%下消失。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Recovery accuracy comparison (N=1319)'\n    rows:\n    - condition: Unpruned SFT\n      accuracy: 81.27%\n      grpo_accuracy: 81.27%\n      delta: 0.00pp\n    - condition: RASP-20% SFT\n      accuracy: 61.49%\n      grpo_accuracy: 60.65%\n      delta: -0.84pp\n    - condition: Standard-20% SFT\n      accuracy: 59.29%\n      grpo_accuracy: 58.91%\n      delta: -0.38pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for each condition. GRPO never exceeds\n    SFT for any condition.'\n  analysis: Universal reward-accuracy decoupling confirmed。但SFT gap (RASP vs Standard)\n    在p=0.25下insufficient to support Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff claim。论文只能claim\n    GRPO failure是universal，而非pruning-method-specific。\n- name: GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO\n    full pipeline'\n  expected_results:\n    grasp_post_prune_accuracy: 0.07\n    grasp_post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n    grasp_post_grpo_step30_accuracy: 0.39\n    grasp_grpo_collapse_step: 5\n    grasp_grpo_final_reward: 0.012\n    grasp_grpo_frac_zero_std_final: 0.97\n  result_rationale: GRASPrune在post-prune (7%)和post-SFT (41%)都远低于RASP(31%→61%)和Standard(27%→59%)。这是因为GRASPrune的gate-based\n    selection在reasoning model上suboptimal——它优化一般loss而非reasoning trace。在worst档下，GRASPrune\n    GRPO会比RASP更快collapse(step 5)，但这不提供diagnostic value因为GRASPrune本身就是inferior pruning，collapse快是trivial结论。这个baseline反而削弱了RASP的novelty——如果所有结构化剪枝方法的GRPO都collapse，那collapse不是RASP-specific\n    insight。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: GRASPrune pipeline comparison'\n    rows:\n    - stage: Post-prune\n      grasp: 7%\n      rasp: 31%\n      standard: 27%\n    - stage: Post-SFT\n      grasp: 41%\n      rasp: 61.5%\n      standard: 59.3%\n    - stage: Post-GRPO\n      grasp: 39%\n      rasp: 60.7%\n      standard: 58.9%\n    - stage: GRPO collapse step\n      grasp: ~5\n      rasp: ~10\n      standard: ~60\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Training dynamics plot: GRASPrune collapses immediately (step 5), joining RASP\n    and Standard in universal GRPO failure pattern.'\n  analysis: 'GRASPrune数据confirms所有structured pruning methods的GRPO都fail，但severity ordering\n    (GRASPrune < RASP < Standard)在worst档下被解释为trivially correlated with post-SFT quality而非redundancy-specific\n    mechanism。Reviewer会argue: ''collapse speed simply tracks model quality, not structural\n    damage type''。'\n- name: Multi-seed Post-prune Eval\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 5 seeds (incl. seed 42) for RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune eval,\n    variance estimation\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.305\n    rasp_20_std: 0.018\n    standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.278\n    standard_20_std: 0.022\n    mean_gap_pp: 2.7\n    paired_t_p_value: 0.15\n    cohens_d: 0.42\n  result_rationale: Post-prune accuracy受calibration sample variance影响。5 seeds下RASP\n    mean ≈ 30.5%, Standard mean ≈ 27.8%, gap ~2.7pp。但std较大(1.8-2.2pp)导致paired-t test\n    p≈0.15。Worst档下reviewers会argue这个gap不足以支持CKA-aware scoring的优越性。Cohen's d=0.42 (medium\n    effect)不够convincing for a core method claim。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Multi-seed post-prune accuracy'\n    rows:\n    - seed: 42\n      rasp: 31%\n      standard: 27%\n    - seed: 123\n      rasp: 29%\n      standard: 28%\n    - seed: 456\n      rasp: 32%\n      standard: 30%\n    - seed: 789\n      rasp: 28%\n      standard: 26%\n    - seed: 1024\n      rasp: 32.5%\n      standard: 28%\n  figures_description:\n  - Box plot showing overlapping distributions of RASP vs Standard across 5 seeds.\n    Medians differ by ~3pp but IQRs overlap.\n  analysis: Multi-seed证据weak。Gap存在但不robust (p=0.15)。在worst档下这strengthens the narrative\n    that CKA-aware scoring的marginal benefit不justify方法复杂度。\n- name: Scoring Ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Ablation: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning at 20% sparsity'\n  expected_results:\n    magnitude_only_accuracy: 0.26\n    gradient_only_accuracy: 0.29\n    random_pruning_accuracy: 0.18\n    rasp_accuracy_ref: 0.31\n    standard_accuracy_ref: 0.27\n    gradient_vs_rasp_gap: 2.0\n    gradient_vs_rasp_p_value: 0.41\n  result_rationale: Worst档下，gradient-only(即Standard的核心——importance scoring)已达到29%，接近RASP的31%。CKA\n    modulation仅额外贡献~2pp，这在N=100下完全不显著(p=0.41)。Magnitude-only(26%)和Standard(27%)几乎相同，说明importance\n    metric差异在post-prune这个极低accuracy regime下noise-dominated。Random(18%)是唯一clearly worse的，但这是trivial——任何informed\n    method都应该beat random。Ablation结果undermine CKA的独立贡献。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Scoring method ablation (20% sparsity, N=100)'\n    rows:\n    - method: RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\n      accuracy: 31%\n      stderr: ±4.6%\n    - method: Gradient-only (I)\n      accuracy: 29%\n      stderr: ±4.5%\n    - method: Standard (importance)\n      accuracy: 27%\n      stderr: ±4.4%\n    - method: Magnitude-only\n      accuracy: 26%\n      stderr: ±4.4%\n    - method: Random\n      accuracy: 18%\n      stderr: ±3.8%\n  figures_description:\n  - Horizontal bar chart with error bars. All informed methods cluster around 26-31%,\n    random at 18%. Error bars heavily overlap for all non-random methods.\n  analysis: CKA modulation的贡献被noise淹没。Worst档叙事：RASP's CKA component is at best marginal\n    (2pp over gradient-only, p=0.41)。不足以支持CKA作为method contribution。\n- name: Per-structure CKA-Recoverability Correlation\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Per-head F(h) vs activation change after recovery, mixed-effects regression\n  expected_results:\n    pearson_r_fh_vs_activation_change: 0.12\n    spearman_rho: 0.09\n    mixed_effects_p_value_fh: 0.31\n    variance_explained_by_fh: 0.014\n    weight_norm_variance_explained: 0.08\n    gradient_importance_variance_explained: 0.11\n  result_rationale: Worst档下，F(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy）与recovery后的activation\n    change几乎无correlation (r=0.12)。Mixed-effects model中F(h)不显著(p=0.31)，且解释方差仅1.4%——远低于简单的weight\n    norm (8%)或gradient importance (11%)。这demolishes CKA作为'predicting recoverability'的诊断工具的claim。如果functional\n    redundancy不predict recoverability，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的机制基础就不存在。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Mixed-effects regression coefficients'\n    rows:\n    - predictor: F(h) (CKA redundancy)\n      beta: '0.034'\n      p_value: '0.31'\n      R²_partial: '0.014'\n    - predictor: Weight norm\n      beta: '0.089'\n      p_value: '0.02'\n      R²_partial: '0.08'\n    - predictor: Gradient importance\n      beta: '0.102'\n      p_value: '0.008'\n      R²_partial: '0.11'\n    - predictor: Activation magnitude\n      beta: '0.076'\n      p_value: '0.04'\n      R²_partial: '0.06'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: F(h) vs activation change, color-coded by layer. No visible trend,\n    points scattered. R²=0.014 annotated.'\n  analysis: CKA-based redundancy metric不predict recovery behavior。在worst档下这是致命的——RASP的理论基础(redundant\n    structures are safely removable for SFT)没有per-structure evidence支撑。\n- name: SFT-only Recovery Comparison\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20), SFT only, same data budget.\n    Tests recovery paradigm interaction.\n  expected_results:\n    sft_rasp_20_accuracy: 0.6149\n    sft_standard_20_accuracy: 0.5929\n    sft_gap_pp: 2.2\n    sft_gap_p_value: 0.25\n    sft_rasp_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n    sft_standard_loss_curve_final: 0.64\n  result_rationale: 这个实验实际上已经完成（plan_002的SFT就是SFT-only recovery）。Worst档下结果不变：RASP\n    61.49% vs Standard 59.29%，gap 2.2pp, p=0.25。Loss curves几乎identical（都converge到0.64）。不显著的SFT\n    gap意味着'CKA-aware pruning benefits SFT recovery'这个claim不成立。如果SFT gap都不存在，Redundancy-Stability\n    Tradeoff（SFT favors removing redundancy, RLVR needs it）的SFT侧就是null。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SFT-only recovery (N=1319)'\n    rows:\n    - method: RASP-20%\n      sft_accuracy: 61.49%\n      sft_loss: '0.64'\n    - method: Standard-20%\n      sft_accuracy: 59.29%\n      sft_loss: '0.64'\n    - method: Gap\n      delta: +2.20pp\n      p_value: '0.25'\n  figures_description:\n  - Loss curves for RASP vs Standard SFT recovery — virtually identical trajectories,\n    both converging to 0.64.\n  analysis: SFT gap不显著。Worst档叙事：无法claim RASP对SFT recovery有advantage，因此Redundancy-Stability\n    Tradeoff的一侧(SFT favors RASP)不成立。\n- name: 25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Full Pipeline\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '25% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both RASP and Standard'\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.21\n    standard_25_post_prune_accuracy: 0.16\n    rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.52\n    standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n    sft_gap_25_pp: 0.75\n    sft_gap_25_p_value: 0.35\n    grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n    grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 6\n    grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.011\n    grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.015\n    grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n    grpo_standard_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.96\n    collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard: 0.67\n  result_rationale: '25%是worst档的critical sparsity。Post-prune: RASP 21% vs Standard\n    16%（已confirmed）。Post-SFT: RASP ~52% vs Standard ~51.25%（已有Standard数据），gap缩小到<1pp\n    (p=0.35)——因为higher sparsity下SFT recovery能力更受限于absolute damage而非which structures\n    were removed。GRPO: 关键——两者都在≤10步内collapse。RASP step 4, Standard step 6，ratio仅0.67（不是20%下的6x差距）。这是因为25%\n    sparsity下两个模型的exploration capacity都已被破坏到临界值以下，collapse变成near-deterministic而非structure-dependent。Severity\n    gradient消失——无法区分''redundancy removal causing fast collapse'' vs ''general over-pruning\n    causing universal collapse''。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 25% sparsity pipeline comparison'\n    rows:\n    - stage: Post-prune\n      rasp_25: 21%\n      standard_25: 16%\n    - stage: Post-SFT\n      rasp_25: 52%\n      standard_25: 51.25%\n    - stage: Post-SFT gap\n      delta: +0.75pp\n      p_value: '0.35'\n    - stage: GRPO collapse step\n      rasp_25: ~4\n      standard_25: ~6\n    - stage: GRPO final frac_zero_std\n      rasp_25: '0.98'\n      standard_25: '0.96'\n  - name: 'Table: Collapse gradient comparison across sparsity'\n    rows:\n    - sparsity: 20%\n      rasp_collapse: step 10\n      standard_collapse: step 60\n      ratio: 6.0x\n    - sparsity: 25%\n      rasp_collapse: step 4\n      standard_collapse: step 6\n      ratio: 1.5x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Training dynamics overlay: RASP-25% and Standard-25% frac_zero_std curves nearly\n    overlapping, both reaching 0.95+ by step 8. Contrast with 20% where curves diverge\n    dramatically.'\n  - 'Collapse ratio vs sparsity plot: ratio drops from 6x at 20% to 1.5x at 25%, suggesting\n    the diagnostic value disappears at higher sparsity.'\n  analysis: '25% sparsity完全消解了collapse severity gradient。两者都太脆弱无法sustain GRPO training。Reviewer会argue:\n    ''你的diagnostic只在一个sparsity点work(20%)，换个sparsity就break——这不是robust mechanism而是coincidence。''\n    SFT gap也shrink到不显著(0.75pp, p=0.35)。Worst档核心结论：Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff在25%下不可观测。'\n- name: 30% Sparsity Probe\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 30% sparsity prune + eval only (no recovery) for RASP and Standard\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.08\n    standard_30_post_prune_accuracy: 0.06\n    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.25\n    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.18\n    gap_pp: 2.0\n    p_value: 0.55\n  result_rationale: 30% sparsity下两者都接近complete collapse (8% vs 6%)。Model基本无法生成coherent\n    reasoning。Gap 2pp在这个regime下meaningless——两者都是catastrophically damaged。这confirms\n    25-30%是DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B structured pruning的hard ceiling，但不提供任何method-differentiating\n    evidence。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 30% sparsity post-prune'\n    rows:\n    - method: RASP-30%\n      accuracy: 8%\n      eos_rate: 25%\n      avg_len: '3200'\n    - method: Standard-30%\n      accuracy: 6%\n      eos_rate: 18%\n      avg_len: '3500'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Sparsity vs post-prune accuracy curve: steep decline from 20% to 30%, both methods\n    converging to near-zero.'\n  analysis: Confirms sparsity ceiling但对method comparison无价值。在worst档下用作evidence that\n    structured pruning has narrow useful range (practical limitation)。\n- name: Extended Evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.48\n    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n    standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.47\n    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n    unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.62\n    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n    rasp_vs_standard_mmlu_p: 0.62\n    rasp_vs_standard_humaneval_p: 0.45\n    rasp_vs_standard_math500_p: 0.38\n  result_rationale: 'OOD benchmarks下RASP vs Standard gap同样不显著。MMLU差1pp, HumanEval差2pp,\n    MATH差2pp——都在noise range内。这是因为SFT recovery是domain-agnostic的(teacher-forcing on\n    GSM8K)，CKA-aware pruning的marginal structural advantage不transfer到其他tasks。Worst档下这进一步confirms\n    RASP无meaningful advantage。同时，pruned vs unpruned的大幅drop (MATH: 52%→27%)表明structured\n    pruning造成的reasoning能力损失是across-domain的。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Extended evaluation'\n    rows:\n    - benchmark: MMLU\n      unpruned: 62%\n      rasp_20: 48%\n      standard_20: 47%\n      gap_pp: +1pp\n      p: '0.62'\n    - benchmark: HumanEval\n      unpruned: 55%\n      rasp_20: 35%\n      standard_20: 33%\n      gap_pp: +2pp\n      p: '0.45'\n    - benchmark: MATH-500\n      unpruned: 52%\n      rasp_20: 28%\n      standard_20: 26%\n      gap_pp: +2pp\n      p: '0.38'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart showing capability profile: unpruned vs RASP-20% vs Standard-20%\n    across 4 benchmarks. Pruned models uniformly degraded, RASP and Standard nearly\n    identical.'\n  analysis: RASP advantage不generalize beyond GSM8K。在worst档下这是expected——如果GSM8K上gap都不显著，OOD上更不可能significant。但pruned\n    models的uniform degradation strengthens 'structured pruning is destructive' narrative。\n- name: Bonsai Baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning at 20% sparsity\n  expected_results:\n    bonsai_post_prune_accuracy: 0.24\n    bonsai_post_sft_accuracy: 0.56\n    bonsai_post_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n    bonsai_grpo_peak_reward: 0.019\n    bonsai_grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.93\n  result_rationale: 'Bonsai是gradient-free方法，通常在structured pruning中accuracy略低于gradient-based方法。Post-prune\n    24% (between random 18% and Standard 27%)。Post-SFT recovery到56%——低于RASP(61.5%)和Standard(59.3%)但仍reasonable。GRPO\n    collapse at step 8——和RASP(step 10)同量级。在worst档下，Bonsai的加入进一步demonstrates所有structured\n    pruning的GRPO都collapse，且collapse speed和post-SFT quality正相关（trivialy: worse model\n    = faster collapse）。不提供redundancy-specific insight。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Method comparison including Bonsai'\n    rows:\n    - method: RASP\n      post_prune: 31%\n      post_sft: 61.5%\n      grpo_collapse: step 10\n    - method: Standard\n      post_prune: 27%\n      post_sft: 59.3%\n      grpo_collapse: step 60\n    - method: Bonsai\n      post_prune: 24%\n      post_sft: 56%\n      grpo_collapse: step 8\n    - method: GRASPrune\n      post_prune: 7%\n      post_sft: 41%\n      grpo_collapse: step 5\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: post-SFT accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all 4 methods. Clear\n    positive correlation (r=0.95) suggesting collapse speed is simply a function of\n    model quality, not pruning mechanism.'\n  analysis: 'Bonsai数据reveals collapse speed几乎perfectly correlates with post-SFT accuracy\n    (r≈0.95)。Worst档下reviewer会argue: ''RASP collapses fast不是因为它removed redundancy,\n    而是因为它happens to produce slightly lower SFT quality than Standard (61.5 vs 59.3,\n    but at 25% the gap disappears and so does the collapse difference)。Collapse is\n    trivially predicted by model quality, not by structural damage type。'''\n- name: CKA Reliability Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: Split-half consistency + calibration size sensitivity\n  expected_results:\n    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.72\n    cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr: 0.78\n    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr: 0.85\n    score_variance_across_splits: 0.15\n    top_20pct_overlap_across_splits: 0.68\n  result_rationale: CKA scores本身有moderate reliability (ρ=0.72 split-half)，不算terrible但也不够high\n    for confident structure selection。Top-20% pruned structures只有68% overlap across\n    splits——意味着32%的pruning decisions是unstable的。Calibration size从256→512→1024确实improves\n    (0.78→0.85)，但512 (我们用的) 仍有notable instability。Worst档下这undermines RASP scoring的reliability——如果CKA\n    scores themselves are noisy，基于它们的pruning decision也是noisy的。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: CKA reliability metrics'\n    rows:\n    - metric: Split-half Spearman ρ\n      value: '0.72'\n    - metric: Cal-256 vs Cal-512 rank corr\n      value: '0.78'\n    - metric: Cal-512 vs Cal-1024 rank corr\n      value: '0.85'\n    - metric: Top-20% set overlap (split-half)\n      value: 68%\n  figures_description:\n  - Heatmap of structure rankings across 5 split-half replications. Visible inconsistency\n    in middle-ranked structures.\n  analysis: CKA reliability是acceptable but not high。32% decision instability在worst档下被interpret为：RASP的marginal\n    advantage可能just是particular calibration sample的artifact而非stable structural property。\n- name: Alpha Sensitivity Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} sweep in RASP scoring at 20% sparsity, post-prune\n    + post-SFT eval\n  expected_results:\n    alpha_0_post_prune: 0.27\n    alpha_0_post_sft: 0.64\n    alpha_0p25_post_prune: 0.23\n    alpha_0p25_post_sft: 0.58\n    alpha_0p5_post_prune: 0.22\n    alpha_0p5_post_sft: 0.55\n    alpha_1p0_post_prune: 0.31\n    alpha_1p0_post_sft: 0.57\n    alpha_2p0_post_prune: 0.36\n    alpha_2p0_post_sft: 0.62\n    optimal_alpha_post_prune: 2.0\n    optimal_alpha_post_sft: 0.0\n    correlation_postprune_vs_postsft: -0.45\n  result_rationale: '已有post-prune数据(α=0:27%, α=0.25:23%, α=0.5:22%, α=1:31%, α=2:36%)。Post-SFT数据在worst档下shows反转：α=0(即Standard，无CKA)给出最高post-SFT(64%)，而α=2(强CKA\n    weighting, 最高post-prune)给出62%。α和post-SFT accuracy无单调关系，且post-prune和post-SFT accuracy\n    negatively correlated (r=-0.45)——高post-prune不predict高post-SFT。这is devastating:\n    RASP的CKA modulation optimizes wrong proxy。保留high-CKA structures helps immediate\n    post-prune accuracy但doesn''t help (甚至slightly hurts) SFT recovery。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Alpha ablation full pipeline'\n    rows:\n    - alpha: 0.0 (=Standard)\n      post_prune: 27%\n      post_sft: 64%\n      post_sft_ci: ±4.7%\n    - alpha: '0.25'\n      post_prune: 23%\n      post_sft: 58%\n      post_sft_ci: ±4.9%\n    - alpha: '0.5'\n      post_prune: 22%\n      post_sft: 55%\n      post_sft_ci: ±5.0%\n    - alpha: 1.0 (=RASP)\n      post_prune: 31%\n      post_sft: 57%\n      post_sft_ci: ±5.0%\n    - alpha: '2.0'\n      post_prune: 36%\n      post_sft: 62%\n      post_sft_ci: ±4.9%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) and α vs post-SFT accuracy\n    (non-monotonic/U-shape). Shows CKA helps post-prune but not post-SFT.'\n  - 'Scatter: post-prune accuracy vs post-SFT accuracy across α values. Negative or\n    null correlation.'\n  analysis: 'α ablation是worst档最damaging的实验。Post-prune accuracy和post-SFT accuracy decouple——CKA\n    optimization of post-prune is a wrong objective。α=0 (no CKA, Standard) achieves\n    highest post-SFT despite lowest post-prune。RASP''s core insight (''remove redundant\n    structures because they''re safely recoverable'') is empirically falsified: recovering\n    redundant-structure-preserving models is NOT easier。'\n- name: Inference Speedup Benchmark\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: Wall-clock latency + throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\n  expected_results:\n    dense_latency_ms_per_token: 18.5\n    rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.2\n    standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 16.0\n    dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 54.1\n    rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 61.7\n    standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 62.5\n    speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.14\n    speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.16\n    memory_reduction_pct: 18.5\n  result_rationale: '20% structured pruning只给14-16% speedup。这是因为：(1) MLP-only pruning\n    (attn groups未被pruned) 限制了speedup ceiling; (2) GPU利用率在batch_size=1时不是memory-bound;\n    (3) Structured pruning的实际speedup远低于theoretical FLOP reduction (20%)因为kernel launch\n    overhead和memory bandwidth不是线性关系。Worst档下1.14-1.16x speedup is disappointing——不足以justify\n    20pp+ accuracy loss (81%→61%)。Reviewer: ''you lose 20pp accuracy for 14% speedup\n    — no practitioner would make this trade。'''\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Inference efficiency'\n    rows:\n    - model: Dense (7.6B)\n      latency_ms: '18.5'\n      throughput: 54.1 tok/s\n      memory_gb: '15.2'\n    - model: RASP-20% (6.2B)\n      latency_ms: '16.2'\n      throughput: 61.7 tok/s\n      memory_gb: '12.4'\n    - model: Standard-20% (6.2B)\n      latency_ms: '16.0'\n      throughput: 62.5 tok/s\n      memory_gb: '12.4'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: speedup factor vs accuracy retention. 1.14x speedup at 76% accuracy\n    retention — poor Pareto position.'\n  analysis: Inference speedup insufficient to justify accuracy cost。Worst档下这weaken\n    practical motivation：如果structured pruning只给14% speedup with 25% accuracy loss，research\n    question本身的relevance被questioned。需要在paper中reframe为'studying fundamental interaction'而非'practical\n    compression method'。\n- name: Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_017\n  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%, eval + SFT → GRPO\n  expected_results:\n    unstructured_20_post_prune_accuracy: 0.72\n    unstructured_20_post_sft_accuracy: 0.79\n    unstructured_20_grpo_accuracy: 0.79\n    unstructured_20_grpo_collapse: false\n    unstructured_20_grpo_steps_stable: 100\n    unstructured_20_grpo_final_reward: 0.55\n  result_rationale: 'Unstructured pruning at 20% preserves大部分accuracy (72% post-prune\n    vs structured 27-31%)因为individual weight zeroing比removing entire structures damage\n    far less。Post-SFT recovery到79%接近dense baseline (81%)。关键：GRPO在unstructured pruned\n    model上NOT collapse——100 steps stable, reward reaches 0.55。这directly refutes ''pruning\n    breaks RLVR''的general claim，narrowing it to''STRUCTURED pruning breaks RLVR''。In\n    worst档: 这是double-edged。一方面narrows scope (only structured matters)；另一方面reviewer可能argue\n    ''if unstructured doesn''t collapse, your finding is about model capacity, not\n    redundancy — 20% structured removes much more effective capacity than 20% unstructured''。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Structured vs Unstructured comparison'\n    rows:\n    - method: Dense\n      post_prune: 81%\n      post_sft: 81%\n      grpo_collapse: 'No'\n      grpo_accuracy: 81%\n    - method: Unstructured-20%\n      post_prune: 72%\n      post_sft: 79%\n      grpo_collapse: 'No'\n      grpo_accuracy: 79%\n    - method: RASP-Structured-20%\n      post_prune: 31%\n      post_sft: 61.5%\n      grpo_collapse: Step 10\n      grpo_accuracy: 60.7%\n    - method: Standard-Structured-20%\n      post_prune: 27%\n      post_sft: 59.3%\n      grpo_collapse: Step 60\n      grpo_accuracy: 58.9%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'GRPO training dynamics: unstructured-20% tracks dense model (no collapse), while\n    all structured methods collapse. Clear dichotomy.'\n  analysis: 'Unstructured doesn''t collapse → GRPO failure是structured-pruning-specific。Worst档下reviewer会reframe为capacity\n    argument: ''structured pruning removes 20% of architecture but >>20% of effective\n    capacity (因为removes entire functional units)，collapse是trivially因为model太弱not因为any\n    specific structural property''。这undermines Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff的mechanistic\n    claim进一步。'\n- name: SFT OOD Eval Contingency\n  plan_id: plan_018\n  description: Standard SFT-recovered model (64%→59.3% GSM8K) on MATH-500 and HumanEval\n  expected_results:\n    standard_sft_math500: 0.22\n    standard_sft_humaneval: 0.28\n    rasp_sft_math500: 0.24\n    rasp_sft_humaneval: 0.3\n    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n    gap_math500_pp: 2.0\n    gap_humaneval_pp: 2.0\n    gap_math500_p: 0.35\n    gap_humaneval_p: 0.4\n  result_rationale: 'OOD evaluation下RASP vs Standard gap同样tiny (2pp, p>0.35)。两个pruned\n    models在harder benchmarks上都heavily degraded vs unpruned (MATH: 22-24% vs 52%, HumanEval:\n    28-30% vs 55%)。这表明SFT recovery在GSM8K-domain外效果很差——recovery是domain-specific pattern\n    memorization而非genuine reasoning restoration。Worst档下这进一步削弱SFT recovery作为practical\n    solution的framing，但不directly影响GRPO failure narrative。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: OOD evaluation'\n    rows:\n    - benchmark: MATH-500\n      unpruned: 52%\n      rasp_20: 24%\n      standard_20: 22%\n      p_value: '0.35'\n    - benchmark: HumanEval\n      unpruned: 55%\n      rasp_20: 30%\n      standard_20: 28%\n      p_value: '0.40'\n    - benchmark: GSM8K\n      unpruned: 81%\n      rasp_20: 61.5%\n      standard_20: 59.3%\n      p_value: '0.25'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Accuracy retention ratio (pruned/unpruned) across benchmarks. GSM8K: 75%, MATH:\n    45%, HumanEval: 53%. Recovery is heavily domain-biased.'\n  analysis: OOD collapse suggests SFT recovery是GSM8K-specific memorization。Worst档下这weakens\n    'SFT-only recovery as practical recommendation'——如果SFT只恢复in-domain performance，recommendation的practical\n    scope极其有限。\n- name: Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 20% SFT Eval\n  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_20\n  description: Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 20% (RASP + Standard), SFT recovery, N=200\n    eval\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n    standard_20_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n    gap_pp: 1.5\n    gap_p_value: 0.42\n  result_rationale: '已有实验数据: RASP 72.5% vs Standard 71%。Gap仅1.5pp (p=0.42)——比DeepSeek-R1上的2.2pp还小。Cross-model下CKA-aware\n    pruning的advantage进一步diminish，因为Qwen-Math的architecture redundancy pattern可能不同于DeepSeek-R1-Distill。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-model 20% SFT'\n    rows:\n    - model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\n      rasp: 61.5%\n      standard: 59.3%\n      gap: +2.2pp\n    - model: Qwen2.5-Math-7B\n      rasp: 72.5%\n      standard: 71.0%\n      gap: +1.5pp\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Cross-model SFT gap even smaller。RASP advantage不robust across models。\n- name: Qwen-Math-7B RASP/Standard 25% Full Pipeline\n  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_25\n  description: Qwen2.5-Math-7B pruned at 25% (RASP + Standard), SFT + GRPO, N=200\n    eval\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n    standard_25_qwen_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n    sft_gap_pp: 1.0\n    sft_gap_p_value: 0.48\n    grpo_rasp_25_qwen_collapse_step: 7\n    grpo_standard_25_qwen_collapse_step: 8\n    grpo_rasp_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.022\n    grpo_standard_25_qwen_peak_reward: 0.025\n    collapse_ratio: 0.875\n  result_rationale: 'Worst档核心: Qwen-Math上GRPO collapse差异消失。RASP step 7 vs Standard\n    step 8——ratio 0.875 (within noise)。两者都rapidly collapse，无severity gradient。这directly\n    falsifies ''collapse speed diagnoses structural damage type'' claim跨模型。原因：Qwen-Math的internal\n    redundancy structure可能不同(more uniform, less exploitable by CKA)，或25% sparsity对Qwen-Math已经是critical\n    threshold (Qwen-Math baseline更高所以25% damage也更severe in relative terms)。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Qwen-Math 25% GRPO collapse comparison'\n    rows:\n    - model: DeepSeek-R1 25%\n      rasp_collapse: step 4\n      standard_collapse: step 6\n      ratio: 1.5x\n    - model: Qwen-Math 25%\n      rasp_collapse: step 7\n      standard_collapse: step 8\n      ratio: 1.14x\n    - model: DeepSeek-R1 20%\n      rasp_collapse: step 10\n      standard_collapse: step 60\n      ratio: 6.0x\n    - model: Qwen-Math 20%\n      rasp_collapse: TBD\n      standard_collapse: TBD\n      ratio: TBD\n  figures_description:\n  - Cross-model collapse dynamics overlay. Qwen-Math RASP and Standard curves are\n    indistinguishable.\n  analysis: Cross-model non-reproducibility是worst档的killshot for mechanism claim。如果collapse\n    gradient只在one model × one sparsity下observe，它不是generalizable mechanism而是coincidence。\n","numLines":728,"startLine":1,"totalLines":728}}}
