ng-specificity of collapse\\\\n    result: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D044\\\\n- id: D046\\\\n  date: 2026-05-16 08:07 UTC\\\\n  summary: Qwen Math calibration=256 不重跑，论文加 footnote 说明差异\\\\n  rationale: 论文 claim 是跨模型现象存在性（collapse 是否发生 + severity gradient 是否复现），不是跨模型绝对数值对比。Calibration\\\\n    256 vs 512 导致 ~5% group selection 差异，但不影响 collapse/non-collapse 的定性判断。重跑需重新计算\\\\n    importance+CKA scores (~2h GPU) + 重新剪枝，收益不值得 DDL 压力下的时间成本。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: prune_rasp_20_qwen_math\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: sparsity 18.99%, 199 MLP groups\\\\n  - exp_id: prune_standard_20_qwen_math\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: sparsity 19.28%, 202 MLP groups\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D045\\\\n- id: D047\\\\n  date: 2026-05-16 09:36 UTC\\\\n  summary: 新增 RASP-RLVR 实验：反转 CKA scoring 保护冗余结构，预防 GRPO collapse\\\\n  rationale: 用户指出纯分析贡献竞争力有限。已证明冗余移除→collapse加速的单调关系，逻辑推论反转scoring（保护冗余）应防止collapse。成本低（复用现有scores，仅改公式符号）、风险低（单调关系已建立）、收益高（论文从analysis升级为diagnosis+remedy）。用户批准\\\\\\\"要做\\\\\\\"。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: grpo_stage2_rasp_20_v9\\\\n    role: motivation\\\\n    result: RASP removes redundancy → collapse step 10\\\\n  - exp_id: grpo_stage2_standard_20_v8\\\\n    role: motivation\\\\n    result: Standard neutral → collapse step 60\\\\n  - exp_id: grpo_unpruned_v2\\\\n    role: motivation\\\\n    result: Full redundancy → no collapse\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D044\\\\n  - D045\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 33560, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tt3sJKPZCCFEpypJ9pznT3","session_id":"87456414-598d-4dd4-8776-aaed1b39d708","uuid":"c51164f0-4235-4e7a-99ae-1492f9ee2c59","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:41:54.230Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XewAfJDNJNh7V4vg1XBC6K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BBWZ4unhFiRhZgHqcQLJoL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for a top ML venue peer review. Your focus: **Novelty and Related Work**. Review standard: top ML venue, ~25% acceptance rate, 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept).\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Structured Pruning Breaks RLVR Alignment: A Systematic Empirical Study of Reasoning Model Compression\"\n\nThe paper studies how structured pruning interacts with GRPO (RLVR) in reasoning LLMs. Two main findings:\n1. GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling: reward increases but greedy-decode accuracy stays flat (even on unpruned models)\n2. GRPO training collapse on structurally pruned models: output diversity collapses within 4-60 steps\n\nModels: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B (primary), Qwen2.5-Math-7B (cross-model)\nPruning methods tested: RASP (CKA-aware), Standard importance, Bonsai, GRASPrune + unstructured baseline\nSparsity: 20%, 25%, 30%\nThe paper also includes a CKA-aware pruning method (RASP) but the paper's own experiments show it provides no significant advantage.\n\nKey results:\n- GRPO reward goes from 0 to 0.661 on unpruned model but accuracy stays 81.27% (identical). This is \"reward-accuracy decoupling.\"\n- All 4 structured pruning methods show GRPO collapse (frac_zero_std > 0.93 within 4-60 steps)\n- Unstructured pruning at same 20% does NOT collapse\n- Collapse speed correlates with post-SFT model quality (r≈0.95), not with any specific structural property\n- RASP's CKA component adds only 2pp over gradient-only (p=0.41)\n- Alpha ablation shows post-prune accuracy anti-correlates with post-SFT accuracy (r=-0.45)\n- Cross-model (Qwen2.5-Math-7B) shows near-identical collapse regardless of method at 25%\n- OOD benchmarks show severe degradation, SFT recovery is domain-specific\n- Inference speedup is only 1.14-1.16x for ~20pp accuracy loss\n\nRelated work section covers:\n- Structured Pruning of LLMs: LLM-Pruner, SliceGPT, Bonsai, GRASPrune\n- RLVR for Reasoning Models: GRPO, Self-Healing, PASER\n- Pruning-Recovery Interaction: RESP, MPruner\n\nThe paper positions itself as: \"first controlled study of prune→SFT→GRPO pipeline for structured pruning of reasoning LLMs.\"\n\n## Your task\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n1. **Novelty assessment**: Are the contributions genuinely new? How significant are the findings?\n2. **Related work coverage**: Are important baselines missing? Is positioning fair?\n3. **Contribution framing**: Are claims well-calibrated to the evidence?\n4. **Significance and impact**: Would the community benefit from these findings?\n5. **Writing quality and clarity**\n\nOutput format:\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, be specific]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, be specific]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Assessment of Novelty\n[Detailed paragraph]\n\n### Assessment of Related Work\n[Detailed paragraph]\n\n### Minor Issues\n[Presentation, writing, etc.]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34934,"cache_read_input_tokens":22955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34934},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87456414-598d-4dd4-8776-aaed1b39d708","uuid":"8060105c-658f-4c92-8097-64798ecf877e"}
